                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "Thanks!\r\n\r\n> Just in case: this approach for adding surrounding will work **only** in Visual mode. In Normal mode there needs to be a target (textobject/motion) after `sa`.\r\n\r\nYes of course, for normal mode I might do some default mapping such as \r\n```\r\nvim.keymap.set({ \"n\" }, \"s(\", \"saiW(\", { remap = true, desc = \"Surround WORD with ()\" })\r\n```",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks!</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Just in case: this approach for adding surrounding will work <strong>only</strong> in Visual mode. In Normal mode there needs to be a target (textobject/motion) after <code class=\"notranslate\">sa</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Yes of course, for normal mode I might do some default mapping such as</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.keymap.set({ &quot;n&quot; }, &quot;s(&quot;, &quot;saiW(&quot;, { remap = true, desc = &quot;Surround WORD with ()&quot; })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">vim.keymap.set({ \"n\" }, \"s(\", \"saiW(\", { remap = true, desc = \"Surround WORD with ()\" })\n</code></pre></div>",
                    "bodyText": "Thanks!\n\nJust in case: this approach for adding surrounding will work only in Visual mode. In Normal mode there needs to be a target (textobject/motion) after sa.\n\nYes of course, for normal mode I might do some default mapping such as\nvim.keymap.set({ \"n\" }, \"s(\", \"saiW(\", { remap = true, desc = \"Surround WORD with ()\" })",
